It's alt:V multiplayer project that uses js-module-v2 api (it's almost the same to v1, but has moved functions to namespaces, e.g. alt.setInterval is now alt.Timers.setInterval).

### Game loop

Craft/find gear, level up abilities, conquer & defend territories, stay at the top of leaderboard.

### Gameplay mechanics

- Material gathering
- Crafting
- Gear
- Leveling
- Vehicles
- Combat
- World events
- Territory control

### Context

The project heavily utilizes vue3 composable api on the server side, client side and webview, which is a rare sight, but reactability is great.
It utilizes stores like [character.store.ts](mdc:altv/src/client/core/store/character.store.ts) to sync data top-down: server -> client -> webview, so whenever we change state of the store on the server, it gets automatically passed down to client and webview.


